Classification: **SAFE; H1/H3**.

This is the correct equal-characteristic treatment. There is no \(1/k!\), exponential/logarithmic series, or inversion of binomial coefficients.

#### B2. Abstract finite-field use is genuinely abstract

> “K_0 := F_Q, K_i := F_{Q^{f_1...f_i}}.”

Classification: **SAFE; criterion (a)**.

Only the finite residue fields and their finite extensions are used. There is no Teichmüller or Witt-vector construction in the displayed ladder grammar.

#### B3. Normalizer recursion is integral combinatorics

> “e_{i+1} m_i(k) + b_i(k) u_{i+1} = k, 0 <= b_i(k) < e_{i+1}  
