### C. `GENTOW4_PROOF_2026-08-09.md`

#### C1. Separability is explicitly fenced

> “f monic of degree n = D'·mu1 on the genre-G opening locus, disc f != 0”

Classification: **SAFE; H5**.

Over any field, including \(\mathbb F_q((t))\), a nonzero discriminant is precisely the needed squarefreeness/separability fence.

#### C2. Drainage peels use that fence honestly

> “if Phi' | f then Phi' EXACTLY divides f (disc != 0)”

> “Phi' | f gives the irreducible factor Phi' itself … exactly once by disc f != 0”

Classification: **SAFE; H5 drainage leg**.

No claim is made that an arbitrary irreducible polynomial is separable. Exact multiplicity one comes from the explicit discriminant hypothesis.

#### C3. Galois block construction remains under the squarefree hypothesis

> “Galois-stability by LEMMA HE7-11, integrality, division of the squarefree f”

