Parity occurs only as a machine tooth in an \(e_2=2\) example. The theorem uses the Newton-slope denominator, which is valuation combinatorics valid at residue characteristic \(2\).

#### C7. Open multiplicity transport is characteristic-neutral

> “At a MIXED side … the TIE mu2* = mu2 is NOT derived here”

> “matching each mu2*(r) to the multiplicity m_r requires the residual-multiplicity transport this corpus has not proved”

