## 4. Slice summary

The local valuation, Newton-polygon, residual-polynomial, cocycle, and finite-field arguments show no genuine mixed-characteristic dependency. In particular, no load-bearing site uses \(1/k!\), \(v(p)<\infty\), \(2^{-1}\), Teichmüller/Witt structure, or silent separability. GENTOW4 is locally equal-characteristic-safe under its explicit discriminant fence. GENTOW2, however, is formally stated only for number-field \(p\)-adic completions, and its quoted FGMN inventory omits the published ambient hypotheses needed to certify replacement by \(\operatorname{Frac}(O)\). GENTOW5 inherits that cite-scope issue and, more decisively, openly leaves \([{\rm GENTOW5-W}(i)]\) unproved for \(i\ge3\), with the governing correction making the general-depth carrier, exact-value, budget, and floor chain conditional. Therefore this slice supports “no new mixed-characteristic mathematics appears necessary,” but it does not establish “the notes already prove the full all-\(O\), all-depth uniformity with no new mathematics.”

